  "comments": [
    {
      "paragraph_index": 1,
      "comment": "Acinetobacter baylyi ADP1 and its mutants were incubated at 30°C, and E. coli at 37°C."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "comment": "Luria–Bertani (LB) medium or minimal medium (MM) (Huang et al., 2005) was used for the cultivation of bacteria as appropriate."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 3,
      "comment": "One litre of MM contains 2.5 g of Na2HPO4, 2.5 g of KH2PO4, 1.0 g of NH4Cl, 0.1 g of MgSO4·7H2O, 10 µl of saturated CaCl2 solution, 10 µl of saturated FeSO4 solution and 1 ml of Bauchop & Elsden solution."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 4,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 5,
      "comment": "1 mL L-1 Bauchop & Elsden solution (1 L contained 10.75 g MgSO4, 4.5 g FeSO4.7H2O, 2.0 g CaCO3, 1.44 g ZnSO4.7H2O, 1.12 g MnSO4.7H2O, 0.25 g CuSO4.5H2O, 0.28 g CoSO4.7H2O, 0.01 g H3BO3, and 51.3 mL concentrated hydrochloric acid)."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 8,
      "comment": ""
    }
  ]
